WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.260
- [Woman] Isn't everything
we're doing in life

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.590
a way to be loved a little more?

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:07.703
- Hi, there.

00:00:07.703 --> 00:00:10.193
I'm Aria, and I'm looking for my soulmate.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.720
I began my search a few months ago,

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.450
and although that story ultimately

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:15.913
didn't have a happy ending,

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.273
I now find myself in Vienna,

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.403
the setting for one of my
favorite films of all time.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:26.250
In Before Sunrise, two strangers
spend one incredible night

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.840
wandering the city together

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.023
before going their separate ways.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.953
And since I'm leaving
Vienna tomorrow morning,

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.211
I figure what better way to
spend my final night here

00:00:36.211 --> 00:00:40.553
than by trying to recreate
that magic with a stranger.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:47.466
Could I ask you a quick question?

00:00:47.466 --> 00:00:48.640
- Yeah, of course.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.310
- So, this is my last night in Vienna,

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.720
and I'm looking for someone
to explore it with me

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:53.870
for the evening.
- Oh.

00:00:54.007 --> 00:00:56.810
(speaking French)

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.220
- I'm going to a birthday party.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.670
- We gotta go home and study.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:00.503
- I'm working.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:01.713
- No, no.

00:01:01.713 --> 00:01:02.704
I'm getting rejected left and right.

00:01:02.704 --> 00:01:05.537
(speaking French)

00:01:07.897 --> 00:01:09.350
This is gonna be harder than I thought.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:10.519
How confident are you feelin' Shoshana?

00:01:10.519 --> 00:01:11.954
Scale of one to 10.

00:01:11.954 --> 00:01:15.773
- Hm, I'm gonna say a solid seven.

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:19.100
- I don't know if you know
MQ, it's MuseumsQuartier.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.570
There's a lot of young people.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:22.570
- I would love to, but
I cannot say for sure.

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.503
- It could be going better,

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.013
but I'm optimistic.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.360
- Alright, let's go to
the Mariahilfer Strabe.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.273
- I only have two hours left.

00:01:30.363 --> 00:01:31.293
- I'm sorry.

00:01:31.293 --> 00:01:32.126
- Okay, well, this is good.

00:01:32.126 --> 00:01:34.780
I get rejected a lot tonight,
it builds up my tolerance.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.190
So sorry to bother you,

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.040
but could I ask you a quick question?

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:40.793
My name's Aria.

00:01:40.793 --> 00:01:41.626
What's your name?

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:43.023
Nice to meet you.

00:01:43.023 --> 00:01:45.034
This is gonna sound crazy, okay?

00:01:45.034 --> 00:01:46.550
It's my last night in Vienna.

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:47.447
I leave tomorrow morning,

00:01:47.447 --> 00:01:49.250
and we're looking to find someone

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.270
to come explore the city with me tonight,

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.963
and I'm wondering if you
would be able to join us.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:55.383
- Sure.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:56.603
- She said sure?

00:01:56.603 --> 00:01:58.420
She said sure.
(laughing)

00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.253
Really, for sure?

00:01:59.253 --> 00:02:00.093
- Of course.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.480
- I don't know if we should cheer.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:04.913
- [All] Yay!

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.541
- This is my first time in Vienna.

00:02:07.541 --> 00:02:08.610
- First time?
- Yeah.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:09.443
- When did you come here?

00:02:09.443 --> 00:02:11.483
- I arrived two days ago.
- Two days?

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:13.000
- Two days ago.
- How did you like it so far?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:13.833
- I love it.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.623
I live in LA, and...
- Okay, I've been there.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:17.860
- Oh, yeah, when were you in LA?

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.240
- Yeah, it's like some years ago,

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.853
but I was there for exchange but not LA.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:26.183
- Oh, really?

00:02:26.183 --> 00:02:27.230
- No, sadly, no.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.712
- What did you go to exchange?

00:02:28.712 --> 00:02:29.545
- Wisconsin.

00:02:29.545 --> 00:02:30.850
- You went to Wisconsin, oh, wow.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.453
So, you're from Vienna, born and raised?

00:02:32.453 --> 00:02:33.580
- Yes, yes, yes.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.623
- Oh, wow, so you must have
some Vienna fun facts to share.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:39.800
- I don't know, it's...

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.670
I don't know, it's just...

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.873
It's so different if you're
raised and live here.

00:02:46.696 --> 00:02:49.037
I don't really have too
much comparison, you know?

00:02:49.037 --> 00:02:50.237
- But you love the city?

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:51.163
- Yes.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:55.740
(speaking Austrian)

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:56.740
Yeah, (speaking Austrian).

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:57.913
- What's a (speaking Austrian)?

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:58.773
- Big beer.

00:02:58.773 --> 00:03:02.484
- Oh, oh my.

00:03:02.484 --> 00:03:03.470
(speaking Austrian)

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.303
- What's it?

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.120
- Like bon appetit.

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.034
- What am I eating?

00:03:07.034 --> 00:03:07.956
(speaking Austrian)

00:03:07.956 --> 00:03:09.700
- Okay, so what is (speaking Austrian)?

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:10.533
- It's meat.

00:03:12.019 --> 00:03:15.602
- (laughs) I can see that.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:18.243
I have to warn you, though,
if I keep drinking this,

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.260
this video's gonna go places.

00:03:21.215 --> 00:03:23.465
(cheering)

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.160
So, what is Scnapps, though?

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.103
- Well, first, just try it
and then I'll explain, maybe.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.097
Other way 'round.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:35.980
I don't know if you'd still like it.

00:03:40.211 --> 00:03:42.461
(coughing)

00:03:42.933 --> 00:03:43.943
- I don't like that.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.033
I'm so sorry.

00:03:45.122 --> 00:03:47.253
I try to be respectful of all cultures.

00:03:47.655 --> 00:03:48.560
(laughing)

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:49.960
How was that for you, Nicki?

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.517
You didn't like it either?

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.010
I need some pretzels.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:57.133
I'm so sorry.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.080
- I think the worst part
about it is it's too strong.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.133
It's like 80 proof.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:04.380
- It's 80 proof?

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:05.387
Are you...
- Yes.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.170
- When I first told my team
about this video, I said oh,

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:10.050
it's gonna be this beautiful piece

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.573
about two people connecting in Vienna.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.520
Less than one hour after meeting you,

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:17.453
I'm gagging on some Schnapps.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.473
- There is different kinds.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.481
- Of connections.
- No.

00:04:21.481 --> 00:04:22.314
Schnapps!

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.640
(laughing)

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:25.910
- This is absolutely not

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.760
like what happened in Before Sunrise.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.933
Ethan Hawke definitely did not
get drunk in Before Sunrise.

00:04:32.987 --> 00:04:35.943
It's just (mumbles) Before
Sunrise to Before I Pass Out.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.540
- [Elena] My aunt lives here.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:40.373
- [Aria] Your aunt lives...

00:04:40.373 --> 00:04:41.206
Do you wanna say hi to your aunt?

00:04:41.206 --> 00:04:42.910
- I actually think she's sleeping by now

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:45.210
because it's...
- It's kinda late.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:46.990
Yeah, it's true, it's almost midnight

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:49.123
and here we are wandering the streets.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:50.270
What I'm gonna miss about Europe

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:51.520
is just how everything's so walkable

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.100
'cause in the US we don't walk anywhere.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.503
- I know, it's so sad.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:57.390
I really...

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:59.160
I missed it when I was there.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.360
The walking...
- When you were in Wisconsin?

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.863
- Yeah, Wisconsin.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.730
- Oh, do you like The Sound of Music?

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:10.063
- Actually, it's not a thing
that Austrians really watch.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.983
- Oh my God.
- I'm so sorry.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.460
- [Aria] So, what do you know
about Saint Stevens Cathedral?

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.880
- [Elena] Oh, you tell me
first and I'm gonna tell you.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.063
- Saint Stevens Cathedral,
very old cathedral,

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:29.130
but apparently it houses, in a crypt,

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:33.340
the organs of Hofburg family royals

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.390
as well as the dead skeletons

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.193
of people who died in the plague.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:38.563
Very romantic.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.980
- I think it's kinda actually sad

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:44.700
that Saint Stevens Cathedral
isn't really that important

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.003
as a Viennese person.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:49.380
We just walk by and we
don't really realize

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:53.110
how important it is
because if you live here,

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:54.810
you just don't really spend

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:56.660
- [Aria] You don't think
about those things.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:57.860
- [Elena] too much time.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.040
- [Aria] Let's be honest, how
crazy did you think I was?

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:07.920
- Well, at first I was like oh my God,

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.620
I feel so sorry because it's raining

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.610
and you were so excited about this,

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:13.950
and I was just so tired

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.620
and I was like oh my God, I can't do this.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:17.010
But you know, you were so nice.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.773
I was like, I have to do this now.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.943
But then it turned out so great,

00:06:22.135 --> 00:06:23.430
and...
- Yeah, how do you feel?

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:24.850
- I really enjoyed the evening.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:25.700
It was so nice.
- Yeah, I think...

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.693
I think I've had a really great time.

00:06:33.038 --> 00:06:36.038
(light piano music)

00:06:39.236 --> 00:06:41.686
- You know, I believe if
there's any kind of god,

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.333
it wouldn't be in any of us.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:48.963
Not you or me, but just this
little space in between.

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:54.603
If there's any kind of
magic in this world,

00:06:54.804 --> 00:06:56.270
it must be in the attempt

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.763
of understanding someone
sharing something.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:04.090
I know, it's almost important to succeed,

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.963
but who cares, really?

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.553
The answer must be in the attempt.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:16.173
- It's sad that I just met
you, but everything has to end.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.663
- But it's worth it, I think.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:20.663
- Yeah.

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:23.690
You're gonna come to LA?

00:07:23.724 --> 00:07:24.557
- Yeah.

00:07:24.732 --> 00:07:26.520
- You're gonna come to LA?
- Definitely.

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:28.373
Just invite me, I'll come.

00:07:28.727 --> 00:07:30.977
(mumbling)

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:35.460
- I think it worked out the
way it was meant to work out.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:36.570
I think there was
something very bittersweet

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:39.130
in the idea that I spent one
great night with a great girl

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:41.833
who I will maybe never see again,

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:43.530
but that's what life is about, right?

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:44.933
It's about making memories.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.680
Yeah, it's about making memories.

00:07:52.219 --> 00:07:54.969
(acoustic music)

00:08:02.595 --> 00:08:04.670
- Hey, Unsolved is on a new
channel, and now your part.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.810
- [Both] Subscribe here.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:06.853
- That was my part.

